      <span class="label">The Studio</span>
      <h2 style="margin-top:16px">When you leave training, two things happen at once.</h2>
      <div class="problems">
        <div class="problem">
          <span class="glyph sq" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3>You lose your company.</h3>
          <p>For years you've worked every day with people who know you, push you and have your back. Then, overnight, you're on your own.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="problem">
          <span class="glyph tri" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3>Your training stops.</h3>
          <p>Acting is a practice. If you're not doing the thing, your ability plateaus, or worse.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="studio-close">
      <div class="answer"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="pts">
          <p>Leeds Actors Studio exists to fix both. It's an affordable place for recent graduates to keep training.</p>
          <p>With <a href="/leedsactorsstudio/company/"><strong>The Company</strong></a> actors will join a group of actors for consistent training and rehearsals, to stay connected, stay sharp and keep growing between jobs.</p>
          <p>With <a href="#classes"><strong>Uta Hagen</strong></a> sessions, actors can improve their technical acting with Uta Hagen's practical exercises. Ten sessions mirror Hagen's 10 exercises, giving actors a rounded, actor-focused process they can take into any rehearsal room, audition or self-tape.</p>
        </div></div>
        <div class="rect-photo"><img class="ph" src="/assets/las/together-1200.webp" srcset="/assets/las/together-700.webp 700w, /assets/las/together-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw" alt="Actors sitting in a row with scripts, sharing a laugh in rehearsal" width="1350" height="894" loading="lazy"></div>
