  <section id="faq" style="padding-top:16px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="label">Questions</span><h2>Before you book</h2></div>
      <div class="faq-wrap">
      <div class="faq">
        <details><summary>Who is Leeds Actors Studio for?</summary><p>Actors who have recently left drama school and want to keep training. Classes are open to anyone with some training or experience.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What's the difference between the Uta Hagen course and the Company?</summary><p>The Uta Hagen course teaches you the technique, step by step, over ten monthly sessions. The Company uses it: a group of 12 actors who meet every Tuesday to work through scene studies, playtexts and make new work, culminating in a public showing.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do I join the Company?</summary><p>By audition or invitation. We hold auditions three times a year, and actors who have taken the Uta Hagen course are especially welcome to apply. If you are interested, please submit your Spotlight or showreel to leedsactorsstudio@gmail.com.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How much does the Company cost?</summary><p>£25 a month covers every Tuesday: about £6 a night. Company nights run every Tuesday, 6–7.30pm, with the first Tuesday of the month as a skills session (free for members).</p></details>
        <details><summary>How does pay-what-you-can work?</summary><p>Classes are priced per 90-minute session at three rates: Reduced £14, Standard £20 and Supporter £26. Choose the one that suits you; there's no proof or explanation needed. Supporter places help us keep reduced places available.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I join the Uta Hagen course partway through?</summary><p>Yes. You can join at any session, or come every month. Just book ahead. Each session is priced at the pay-what-you-can rates.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What happens in an Audition Surgery?</summary><p>A mock audition with detailed feedback and direction. Bring your own speech, or choose one of the 3–4 speeches we release each month.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is 1:1 coaching online or in person?</summary><p>Mostly online, with sessions in Leeds if arranged in good time.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do I book Drama School Admissions coaching?</summary><p>Book online: choose your tier and pay a £50 deposit or the full fee, then pick a time for your first session. The deposit is non-refundable and comes off the full fee.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can I cancel or move a 1:1 session?</summary><p>You can move a session free of charge up to 24 hours before it starts. Sessions cancelled with less than 24 hours' notice, or missed, can't be refunded. The £50 Drama School Admissions deposit is non-refundable.</p></details>
      </div>
